  "chapter": {
    "number": 11,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          "False balances are an abomination before the Lord: but a just weight is acceptable to him."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          "Wherever pride enters, there will be also disgrace: but the mouth of the lowly meditates wisdom."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "noteId": 44
          },
          "When a just man dies he",
          {
            "noteId": 45
          },
          "leaves regret: but the destruction of the ungodly is speedy, and causes joy."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "noteId": 46
          },
          "Possessions will not profit in a day of wrath, but righteousness will deliver from death."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          "Righteousness",
          {
            "noteId": 47
          },
          "traces out blameless paths: but ungodliness encounters unjust dealing."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          "The righteousness of upright men delivers them: but transgressors are caught in their own destruction."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          "At the death of a just man his hope does not perish: but the boast of the ungodly perishes."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          "A righteous man escapes from a snare, and the ungodly man is delivered up in his place."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          "In the mouth of ungodly men is a snare to citizens: but the understanding of righteous men is prosperous."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          "In the prosperity of righteous men a city prospers:",
          {
            "noteId": 48
          },
          "but by the mouth of ungodly men it is overthrown."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "noteId": 49
          },
          "At the blessing of the upright a city shall be exalted."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          "A man void of understanding sneers at his fellow citizens: but a sensible man is quiet."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          "A double-tongued man discloses the secret counsels of an assembly: but he that is",
          {
            "noteId": 50
          },
          "faithful in spirit conceals matters."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          "They that have no",
          {
            "noteId": 51
          },
          "guidance fall like leaves: but in much counsel there is safety."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          "A bad man does harm wherever he meets a just man: and he hates the sound of safety."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          "A gracious wife",
          {
            "noteId": 52
          },
          "brings glory to her husband: but a woman hating righteousness is a theme of dishonor. The slothful come to lack: but the",
          {
            "noteId": 53
          },
          "diligent support themselves with wealth."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          "A merciful man does good to his own soul: but the merciless destroys his own body."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          "An ungodly man performs unrighteous works: but the seed of the righteous is a reward of truth."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          "A righteous son is born for life: but the persecution of the ungodly ends in death."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          "Perverse ways are an abomination to the Lord: but all they that are blameless in their ways are acceptable to him."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          "He that unjustly strikes hands shall not be unpunished: but he that sows righteousness he shall receive a faithful reward."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          "As an ornament in a swine's snout, so is beauty to an ill-minded woman."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 23,
        "content": [
          "All the desire of the righteous is good: but the hope of the ungodly shall perish."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 24,
        "content": [
          "There are some who scatter their own, and make it more: and there are some also who gather, yet have less.",
          {
            "noteId": 54
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 25,
        "content": [
          "Every sincere soul is blessed: but a passionate man is not graceful."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 26,
        "content": [
          "May he that hoards corn leave it to the nation: but blessing be on the head of him that gives it."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 27,
        "content": [
          "He that devises good counsels seeks good favor: but as for him that seeks after evil, evil shall overtake him."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 28,
        "content": [
          "He that trusts in wealth shall fall; but he that helps righteous men shall rise.",
          {
            "noteId": 55
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 29,
        "content": [
          "He that deals not graciously with his own house shall inherit the wind; and the fool shall be servant to the wise man."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 30,
        "content": [
          "Out of the fruit of righteousness grows a tree of life; but the souls of transgressors are cut off before their time."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 31,
        "content": [
          {
            "noteId": 56
          },
          "If the righteous scarcely be saved, where shall the ungodly and the sinner appear?"
        ]
      }
    ],
